WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:01.968
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.734
We are hanging out with
Tiffany Haddish!

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.267
Her new show, "The Afterparty,"

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.234
premieres this Friday
on Apple TV+.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.968
The show takes place on the
night of a high school reunion.

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.100
Have you ever gone back to
your high school reunion?

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.734
Or gone to one?
-Oh, definitely.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.000
I've been to
my high school reunions.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.534
This is how you know
you made it, Jimmy.

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:24.567
They schedule the reunions
around my schedule.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.667
They call, they like, "Tiffany,
you coming to the reunion?"

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:30.734
I'm like,
"When is it? When is it?"

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.400
They're like,
"When are you available?"

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.534
I'm like,
"She made it, she ready.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.200
Okay, so here are my days."

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.667
We even had one of the reunions,
our 15th reunion,

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:41.100
the year 15, we had it
at the comedy club.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.634
I was like, "Ooh, that night,
I got to do a show."

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:43.701
They was like,
"Where's the show at?"

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.033
I was like,
"Flappers in Burbank."

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.834
They were like, "That's where
the reunion will be."

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.234
-No way.
So you got to see everyone

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.000
from your high school
in the crowd?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.267
-Yeah, every -- It was everybody
from high school.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:56.067
So it kind of turned into
like an impromptu roast.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.434
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:59.567
-So, it was good.
-I've done that too.

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:00.834
I remember doing stand-up,

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:02.968
and my principal came to see me
do stand-up.

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:06.501
And he was like, "Hi, you
remember me?" or whatever.

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:08.167
I go, "Oh, my -- Yeah."
And then I was like,

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.634
"I don't have any material
to make fun of you, but I will."

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.167
-You didn't make fun of
the principal?

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.467
-I couldn't -- I couldn't --

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.167
I didn't have material
about the pr-- He liked me.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:18.033
He was a great -- I was, like,
the kid in school that I --

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.367
If I would get in trouble

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:20.534
and then the principal would be
like, "What did you do?"

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:21.868
I'd go, "I made a joke
or something."

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.434
He was like, "Ah, do you want to
go to detention?"

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.634
I go, "Sure."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.701
Yeah, we just had a deal.
We had an understanding.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.334
I was hanging out in the office.

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:31.100
And I would go to
the principal's office

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.634
and just say, "What's up?"
and hang out.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.367
-My principal at --
Let me tell you something.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.701
When I was in school,
I used to get sent

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:38.167
to the principal's office often.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.300
But see, I was a businesswoman.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.868
And one day I got sent to
the principal's office

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:46.567
because I decided to quit
being the mascot,

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:48.400
and they needed me
back on the field

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.968
'cause the numbers
was dropping low.

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:51.501
The morale was dropping low.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:55.400
And so we had negotiated a deal,
because I would throw out candy

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.100
and I would get the candy
from my home girl

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.100
who worked at the 99-cent store,
right?

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.000
And she owed me some favors

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.234
'cause I would babysit
or whatever.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.901
But anyways, I told him, "Look,

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.267
I can't get back on the field

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.534
unless I get paid,
because I need a boyfriend.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.367
I don't have no boyfriend.
I need to get my hair done

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.400
and my nails done
so I can get a boyfriend."

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.968
And then he was like, "I can't
pay you to be a mascot."

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.834
I said, "Well, look, we got to
figure out something."

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:20.534
So by the time we finished
negotiating, you know,

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:23.801
I was making about, you know,
$50 to $100 a game.

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.200
-See, that's what I'm
talking about.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:28.667
You were the mascot of the team?

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.667
What was the mascot?

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:31.667
What was it?

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.300
-Oh, it was a conquistador.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.934
I was a Spanish soldier,
darling, full garb.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:38.601
-Wow, wow, the conquistador.

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:41.200
And you had to wear a full
costume and everything?

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.701
-Yeah, I wore the full costume,
but I did not wear the head

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:46.801
'cause the head --
it was an old costume.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.834
You know, the school was built
in the '50s.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:52.767
I graduated in the 1990s --
1900s.

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:54.801
Anyways.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:58.067
The head was not a good smell,
so I didn't wear the head.

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:01.667
It was full costume but my head.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.434
And I was the only talking
mascot in the Valley.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.033
I'd be like, "El Ca-- What?!

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.367
And everyone would be like,
"Mino!"

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.033
I went to El Camino Real.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.601
"El Ca-- What?"
"Mino!"

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:12.133
"Who know? We know! Baby!"

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.634
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:18.501
-That's how you do it.

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:20.400
I want to talk about
"The Afterparty."

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.000
It's on this Friday, Apple TV+.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.801
How do we set it up
for everybody? What do we say?

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:29.033
-So, if you love to play
the game "Clue," right?

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.234
Remember the game "Clue"?
-Of course, love it.

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:32.133
-So it's a mystery show,

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:37.300
and every episode is a different
genre of TV and movie.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.100
So the first episode
is the rom-com.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.567
And another episode is
a thriller or action.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:48.467
And, you know, it's just fun.

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.801
It's just a really fun show.
Show them the clip.

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.033
Show them the clip.
-Yeah, here we go.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.200
I want to show the clip.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.033
Here's Tiffany Haddish
in "The Afterparty."

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:57.100
Take a look at this.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.334
-Culp, good.
I need somebody to --

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.367
-Captain called me.
-Really?

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.501
I didn't know you guys
were friends.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:03.767
-Oh, we're not.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.934
He just wanted me to hear it
directly from him

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:07.300
that this is not our case.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.334
He only wanted us to collect
witness statements

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:10.734
until Jermaine got here.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:14.434
-Okay, so that is basically what
he said to me as well,

00:04:14.434 --> 00:04:16.701
but look, I can crack
this thing, okay?

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.100
-You lied to me.
-You're being dramatic.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.501
-Do not call me dramatic!

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:24.033
-It's cool. Look, if I don't
solve this case,

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.934
I promise you
I will take the rap.

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:29.033
I will not let any harm
come to you.

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:32.667
But this ringer guy that's
coming, I know him.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.734
And he will...this up.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.634
Now, I'm not asking you
to help me.

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:40.467
I'm just asking you to not
not help me, okay?

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:43.434
-Yeah, "I'm just asking you
to not, not."

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:45.367
Tiffany Haddish, everybody.
-"Not, not help me."

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:48.968
-"The Afterparty" premieres
Friday on Apple TV+.

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:49.968
We love you, bud.

